# SYNC SIBLINGS (BL-174) — the two `.claude/*.txt` sidecar ignore lines below
# (.claude/last-checked-commit.txt and .claude/last-gate-pass.txt) have TWO
# writers and no mechanical lockstep check: this template, which reaches a
# project only through init.sh's generate_gitignore(), and the idempotent
# upgrade-path backfill marked `# BL-174-GITIGNORE-BACKFILL` in
# scripts/upgrade-project.sh's `_run_idempotent_backfill`, which appends the
# same two exact lines to an ALREADY-scaffolded project. Change one, change the
# other IN THE SAME COMMIT — the backfill matches with `grep -qxF`, so an edit
# here that is not mirrored there silently stops upgraded projects from ever
# receiving the line (which is the BL-174 defect itself, reintroduced). Same
# convention as the `# BL-084-TIER-KEY` SYNC-SIBLINGS predicate.
#
# BL-030 operational state — the detection baseline file. Not project
# content. Updated by scripts/detect-out-of-band-commits.sh on every
# SessionStart and by scripts/reconfigure-project.sh / init.sh after
# state mutations. Tracking it (a) dirtied the working tree on every
# detector run, and (b) made init.sh impossible to finish with a clean
# tree, because the file can never point to its own commit hash.
.claude/last-checked-commit.txt

# BL-161 operational state — the terminal-commit gate-ran receipt. Written by
# .git/hooks/framework-gate.sh on every CLEAN strict-mode terminal commit as proof
# the gate reached its PASS terminal. Not project content, and (like its sibling
# above) it can never point at its own commit — tracking it left the working tree
# perpetually one row/line dirty on the final commit of every session
# (Dogfood-4 F-DF4-007). The audit trail of REAL events (bypass / blocked /
# out-of-band / enforcement-level) still lives in the TRACKED .claude/bypass-audit.json.
.claude/last-gate-pass.txt
